text:
Listen, Josefa, to one who wishes you well,

        for this human life is Villa-nueva,

        and tomorrow it will pass to Villa-flor,

        a flower that flatters the sun it gazes on.


        Peña-fiel does more for the one who desires,

        if at fairs Feria gives you Pastrana,

        for the devil walks loose in Cantillana,

        and in Barca-rota your fortune is employed.


        For this mad Court is Río-seco;

        Saldaña already carries brackish water,

        which pricks pleasure and provokes love;


        for time disillusions your husband,

        for much presumption with little age

        lies about worth and deceives love.


        For if you plant, you will find

        easy Alcañices, not Olivares.
